# Bike Wars, the external port (examples/bike-wars), played on the driver's
# virtual frames. A new game asks for no frame until the space bar; the
# driver cannot type " ", so `Spacebar`, which ohanhi/keyboard's
# `whitespaceKey` reads as the same `Spacebar` key, starts it.
frames
key body Spacebar
frames
# Each frame is 100 ms: a bike moves 0.1 px a millisecond, 10 px a frame,
# and its trail is drawn to where it was a frame before.
frame 2 100
# Red steers with a, d and w, which `Keyboard.Arrows.arrowKey` reads as
# `Character`s with their case kept, so a shifted A turns nothing.
key body a
key body A
key body ArrowRight
frame 2 100
# Red fires its MegaBlaster north, green its AssaultBazooka north: each
# explosion lands at the arena's border.
key body w
key body ArrowUp
frame 3 100
# Red rides into its own blast before it fades: green wins.
frame 5 100
# The frames go on while an explosion burns, and so does green, which
# reaches the border: the game the original declares won becomes a draw.
frame 10 100
frames
# The space bar starts a new game.
key body Spacebar
frame 1 100
